--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. The application is a single HTML file built from the sources in this
repository: HTML and CSS written for this project, a translation table with
four locales, and plain JavaScript. It bundles no library, no framework, no
analytics and no font file, and it loads nothing from the network at runtime -
not even a CDN copy of anything.

The colour maths implemented here (sRGB/HSL/HSV/CMYK conversions, WCAG 2.x
relative luminance and contrast ratio, the Machado, Oliveira and Fernandes
2009 colour vision deficiency matrices, CIE Lab conversion, deterministic
k-means++ palette extraction and the CSS named colour table) is written for
this project from the published public specifications. It does not include
code from any colour library.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
External services
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. Images are decoded and sampled inside the browser; the extracted
palette never leaves the device. Exported files are produced locally and
handed to the download manager of the browser or to the clipboard.
